commit 204ffbb96ef6f6502e126e93f671628b823c988f
Author: agent <agent@nucleus.local>
Date:   Sat Nov 14 23:05:27 2026 +0000

    fix: the integral lift locus reads its cosets in the section's own Smith coordinates (#405, #452)
    
    `integral_parameter_classes` reported the union of the cosets of the wrong
    coordinate lattice, so its locus held classes whose lift is not integral: at
    Sterk's (4.3.8) line of card 029J the 65th class in iteration order had no
    integral restriction (#405), and the smallest control that showed it was
    `U(2) + U(2) + <2>`, where all 64 classes of `P/mP` were reported while 32 of
    them lift.  Two defects, both inside the locus' own computation:
    
    * The section's coordinate matrix was filled from one column per parameter
      generator by *row*, so its (12, 10) shape scrambled the coordinates it then
      read a Smith form off: `smith = (1,1,1,1,1,1,2,2,2,8)` instead of ten ones.
      The columns are now placed by row (`columns[column][entry]`, entry outer) and
      the reading states once that the j-th column is the image of the j-th
      parameter generator.
    * The Smith coordinate change was inverted.  `N A = U^-1 D V^-1`, so `s(a)` in
      `L'` is `(V^-1 a)_i` in `step_i Z` and the class representatives are `a = V u`
      for `u` in the residue range; the code enumerated `a = V^-1 u`.  The
      representatives, the kernel `K = {a : s(a) in L'}` and the parameters of `K`'s
      generators are now read in that one coordinate system, and the docstring
      states the reading, the kernel, and the reason `K` is not the locus at
      divisibility two (Gritsenko--Hulek--Sankaran, arXiv:0810.1614, section 3.1:
      equation (4), printed p. 8; equation (5), p. 9; equation (10), p. 9).
    
    The per-class lift test is now the owned mathematics instead of a coordinate
    matrix product: the lift is `eichler_transvection(f, s(a)) * base` -- the same
    operation `parameterization` composes -- and integrality is that composition's
    own `integral_restriction`.  The hand-rolled product was also transposed, which
    is what let a coset whose lift is not integral pass.
    
    `integral_kernel_group_generators` no longer lists the locus' classes (16
    passing representatives times 16384 kernel classes at this line, each through
    `preimage`, which is why it never returned): the parameter group of the
    integral kernel is generated by the differences of the locus' representatives,
    by the generators of the transvection kernel, and by the period's generators,
    so the family is those, at most `prod_i gcd(step_i, m) + 2 rank` of them (275
    at this line).
    
    `IsotropicVectorReductionImage.kernel_generators` now reads K_v from that owner
    -- the kernel of the identity reduction's rational lift torsor at the line is
    K_v -- and the parallel construction of 5af2f0b576 is gone with it: the Gram
    matrix by a double comprehension over `lattice.b`, the hand-written
    transvection matrix, the private `_isometry_from_column_matrix` call, the
    enumeration of all `d^rank` residue classes and the matrix integrality test.
    `kernel_discriminant_image` and the criterion are unchanged; the class docstring
    now states that the quotient of the two lifts of a wall reflection is
    `E(v, a/2)` (not `-a/2`: equation (4) at `q(a) = -4` gives
    `y + b(v,y)(a+v)/2 - b(a,y)v/2`), and that `K_v` is abelian by equation (5),
    which is what `_kernel_coset_representatives`'s left translates use.
    
    Measured on the tree of eb07c43 with the corrected reading, at the line through
    Sterk's `2e' + f' + alpha-bar_1` on `T_En` (.tmp/qc-evidence/issue452-locus-cosets.log):
    period 4, denominator 2, Smith form ten ones, 1024 representatives of `P/S`,
    256 of them passing, kernel `|K| = 1024`, locus 4^9 classes; every one of the
    275 family members is integral, `rho(K_v)` has order 256 -- the order the
    removed parallel construction reached -- and a passing class plus a kernel
    generator stays integral while a refused class plus the same kernel generator
    does not.  This line's base point is itself integral, so its locus is the
    subgroup of index 4 that the count exhibits.
    
    The control that reproduces #405 on eb07c43 is
    `U(2) + U(2) + <2>` (.tmp/qc-evidence/issue452-controls.log): 64 reported, 32
    integral.  It is now a test.
    
